WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.934
-We're about to play
"Misname That Song."

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:05.334
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:08.334
-♪ Misname That Song ♪

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:11.534
♪ Misname That Song ♪

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.834
-Now I'm gonna need some help,
so joining me now

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:16.267
is the co-host
of the new competition series,

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:19.901
"Baking It," premiering
this Thursday on Peacock,

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.434
please welcome Maya Rudolph!

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:23.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.367
-♪ Misname That Song ♪

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:30.234
♪ Misname That Song ♪

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.567
-Oh, my.
You look fantastic.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.634
Thank you for being here.
I appreciate it, bud.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.701
-Hey, buddy, how are you?
-I'm great.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.300
Let me explain
how this game works.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.868
Okay, in front of each of us

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:44.100
are the incorrect names
of a number of famous songs.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.200
Okay?
All these names are close

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.934
to the actual name of the song
but not quite right.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.601
So when it's your turn,
you're gonna read out

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:53.868
the messed-up version
of that song title,

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:56.334
then the other person tries to
guess the correct song title

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:58.033
based only on that clue.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:00:59.701
We have to guess
as many songs as possible

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.834
before the timer runs out.

00:01:01.834 --> 00:01:03.467
Ready for this?

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:06.367
-You're making it sound
like it's easy.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:07.701
It's hard.

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:09.767
-It is hard, but I don't know
what they're gonna be.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.434
I don't plan it.
But I think you'll --

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:12.634
We'll be good at this.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:13.734
We've done music things
together.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:14.801
-Correct.
-We're good partners.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.300
All right.
-Right.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.934
-Since you're the guest,
you're gonna guess first.

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:20.968
You're gonna get 45 seconds
on the clock,

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.033
and I'm gonna give the clues.

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.067
I think we're gonna do this.
Ready?

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.868
We'll work as a team.
Here we go, bud.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.100
-Okay.
Who's first?

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.701
-I'll start going
and see how many we can get.

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:33.701
-Okay, go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.567
-All right. Ready?
-Yep.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.968
-Here we go.
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:41.734
Okay.
"Pelvic Bones Tell the Truth."

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.133
-"Hips Don't Lie."
-That's correct!

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:44.400
That's exactly
how you play the game.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:51.467
"Not Particularly Taxing
on Myself."

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.868
-What?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.467
-It's a really new song.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:58.200
♪ Taxing ♪

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.901
I'm gonna pass.
I'm going to pass that one.

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:02.200
Passing.
Go.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.968
"I Would Like
to Experience Rhythmic Movement

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.868
with Another Human."

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.033
-"I Wanna Dance With Somebody"!

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.868
-That's correct!
Oh, you know how to do this.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:17.400
"Liquid Atop
Movie Theater Popcorn."

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.133
-Water --
-No. Water?

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:21.968
[ Wah wah! ]

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.267
Close.
"Butter."

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.834
-You said liquid.
-"Butter."

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:28.634
Liquid atop
movie-theater popcorn.

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.934
Butter?
-Oh, I thought you meant

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:34.033
a top movie-theater chain.
I said the Regal.

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.567
-Regal.
It is a top movie-theater chain.

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.734
-It's the most
premier movie chain

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:44.567
in all of the United States.
-Last time we were on the show,

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:48.267
we always play "What is the most
premier movie chains?"

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.400
-And I can't
stop talking about the Regal.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.868
-All right, Maya.
We got two there.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.467
-I got Regal socks.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.067
I told you
I'm great at this game.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.133
-No, this is good.
Because two is great.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.567
Two is -- And, again, we're
partners, so this is beatable.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.000
So now it's my turn.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.734
We'll put another 45 seconds
on the clock.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.767
And whenever you're ready,
read the misnamed song title,

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:10.534
and I will guess.
-Okay.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:13.334
Are you ready?
-Yes.

00:03:13.334 --> 00:03:17.567
-"Pleasant Shakiness."

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:21.501
-Nice -- nice --
-"Pleasant Shakiness."

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.934
Pleasant...
-Fun?

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:26.267
-...Shakiness.
-"Hippy Shake"?

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.133
[ Laughter ]
"Rattle"?

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.100
"Shake, Rattle, Roll"?
Pass.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:34.534
-Shakiness or another kind of --
Do you want me to pass?

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:37.033
-Yeah, pass.
-Okay.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:41.367
"Tequila-Forward Cocktail Town."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.000
You got this.
-Oh, "Margaritaville."

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.868
[ Ding! ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.868 --> 00:03:49.334
-"I Appreciate
the Popular Style of Music

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:51.801
Driven by
Loud Guitar and Vocals."

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.334
-"I Love Rock 'n' Roll."
[ Ding! ]

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:56.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:56.434 --> 00:04:00.834
-"Female Jelly."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:03.067
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:05.367
-What?
-I just wanted to talk

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.767
to you today about female jelly,
that's all.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.834
[ Laughter ]
-No, no, no.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:12.634
Let's talk about
different movie-theater chains.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:16.300
-It was "Lady Marmalade."
-Ah!

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.200
Yeah, "Lady Marmalade."
Okay, all right, look.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.901
We're tied.
That means we're in the zone.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:23.601
-That means we're going
for the death sequence.

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:25.033
-This is the death sequence,
what they call --

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:28.033
We changed the name
to call it the fun round.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:30.868
For this last round,
we're gonna see how many songs

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.200
we can name together.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.400
We're gonna take turns naming
a song and then guessing.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.934
I will start us off
by reading the first clue.

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:40.567
-Okay.
-Here we go.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:43.801
"Ponder Barrier."

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:44.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:47.667
-"Think Wall"?
-Something --

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.567
-"Wonderwall."
-Yes, that's right! Correct.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:52.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.801
-"You Are the Only Thing
on my Holiday Wish List."

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:56.100
-"All I Want for Christmas
Is You."

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.801
[ Ding! ]
-Yes!

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:04.400
-"Slap Bass Above 59th Street."

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.901
-Slap -- Funk.
Funk?

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:10.033
-What kind of funk?
Where's above 59th street?

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:11.634
-"Uptown Funk"!
-That's right!

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:14.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:17.534
-"I Prefer It
in that Particular Manner."

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:19.734
-♪ "I Want It That Way" ♪

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.133
That's what I'm talking about!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:23.267
That is Maya Rudolph
right there.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:24.300
We make a pretty good team.

